{title: 271 - Break Thou the Bread of Life}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #271 • BREAD OF LIFE • 9.11.8.10}
{lyricist: Mary A. Lathbury}
{composer: William F; Sherwin}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 271}
{meta: tune BREAD OF LIFE}
{meta: meter 9.11.8.10}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Break Thou the bread [G]of [F#m]life, [D]dear Lord, tome,
[D]As Thou didst break the [Em]loaves [F]beside [Em]thesea;
[A7/G]Beyond [F#m]the [A7/E]sacred [G/D]page [D]I [A/C#]seek [Em]thee, Lord;
[D/F#]My [A7/E]spirit [Em/G]pants for Thee, OLiving [D]Word!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Bless thou the truth, [G]dear [F#m]Lord, [D]to me, to [A]me,
[D]as thou didst bless [Em]the [F#m]bread [F]by [A/E]Galilee;
[A7/G]then [F#m]shall [A7/E]all [G/D]bondage [D]cease, [A/C#]all [Em]fetters [A]fall;
[D/F#]and [A7/E]I [D]shall [Em/G]find my peace, my [A]all [A7]in [D]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Thou art the bread [G]of [F#m]life, [D]O Lord, to [A]me;
[D]Thy holy Word [Em]the [F#m]truth [F]That [A/E]saveth me;
[A7/G]Give [F#m]me [A7/E]to [G/D]eat [D]and live [A/C#]With [Em]Thee above;
[D/F#]Teach [A7/E]me [D]to [Em/G]love Thy truth, For [A]Thou [A7]art [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Spirit and life [G]are [F#m]they, [D]Words Thou dost [A]speak;
[D]I hasten to [Em]obey, [F]But [A/E]I [Em]am [A]weak;
[A7/G]Thou [F#m]art [A7/E]my [G/D]only [D]help, [A/C#]Thou [Em]art my [A]life;
[D/F#]Heeding Thy [Em/G]holy Word I [A]win [A7]the [D]strife.
{end_of_verse}
